  "result": "The rule and its witnesses for `LVMC_11_52_340` are written, and the gate returned **OK** on the first run (1 of 6 runs used).\n\n**The rule**, in `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_52_340.lean`:\n- **Who it covers:** any vehicle, through the aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** the vehicle is not a City vehicle, and it is in a parking space designated `municipal`.\n- **What it requires:** for every municipal space the vehicle is in, the vehicle is not parked there, using `drv_motion_parked` with `p.halt_speed_tolerance` and `p.parking_min_duration`.\n\n**One choice the node left open:** a City vehicle is read as \"an official vehicle whose kind is municipal\". For an ordinary car the kind field is empty, so checking the kind alone would leave the exception unknown for every private car. Requiring the official-vehicle class as well makes the exception false for them. Both checks come from the node's own `ru.official_vehicle` claim, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses**, in `library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_52_340.lean`:\n- **forbid** (violated): a private car rests in the municipal space for 10 minutes.\n- **permit** (compliant): a private car stops for 30 seconds, then leaves.\n- **idle** (not applicable): a municipal official vehicle rests in the space for an hour.\n- **blind** (unknown): a private car rests beside the space, and whether it is in the space is not observed.\n- **branch_1** (not applicable): a private car rests in a general-designation space.\n- **branch_2** (violated, added by me): a tow truck, which is official but not municipal, parks in the municipal space. Without it, no witness would test the \"municipal\" check on its own.\n\nThe run log and these choices are recorded in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
